 ## Overview
-Independent Block Encoding is a local data compression pass where a volume is divided into independent sub-blocks, each encoded separately, potentially using a global representation learned in a preprocessing step [S1]. It solves the problem of compressing large volumetric datasets for GPU-based rendering by ensuring that memory usage during encoding remains independent of the total input size, while allowing linear scaling and easy parallelization [S2]. It builds on [Stripe-based On-the-fly Decoding](5363-stripe-based-on-the-fly-decoding.md) by preparing compressed blocks for on-the-fly GPU reconstruction.
